<LegalLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="The necessary session cookie and cookieless measurement used by Brev today.">
<h2>1. What Brev uses today</h2>
  <p>Brev uses one necessary technical cookie, <code>brev_session</code>, and cookieless statistics on the public website. There are no non-essential cookies, so there is no cookie consent banner.</p>

  <h2>2. The session cookie</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Type</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td><code>brev_session</code></td><td>Session and authentication.</td><td>Until logout, session expiry or revocation, according to the configured session duration.</td><td>Necessary technical cookie, first-party.</td></tr></tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax. It is Secure in production, where <code>SECURE_COOKIES=true</code>. It is invalidated and deleted when the account is deleted or the session is revoked. It is not used for measurement or advertising.</p>

  <h2>3. Cookieless measurement</h2>
  <p>Plausible is self-hosted on the controller's infrastructure at novezero.it, under the same controller. It measures the landing and legal pages only. It uses no cookies, performs no profiling and retains no personal data.</p>
  <p>IP addresses are used only to derive country and are not retained. No analytics data is transferred to third parties. There is no website analytics in the authenticated dashboard. Link click statistics are described separately in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>4. No browser storage, no tracking</h2>
  <p>The dashboard uses neither localStorage nor sessionStorage. It persists no browser data beyond the session cookie.</p>
  <p>The public landing has no advertising pixels or third-party tracking scripts. Its analytics script is hosted on the controller's own infrastructure. Fonts are self-hosted; Google Fonts is not loaded.</p>

  <h2>5. Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>You can manage or delete cookies in your browser settings. Disabling the session cookie prevents login and access to protected features.</p>

  <h2>6. Future services</h2>
  <p>If services that set cookies or use similar technologies are introduced, such as a payment provider, they will be documented before activation. Where required, consent will be obtained before activation.</p>
</LegalLayout>
